{"id": "EUVD-2026-72690", "enisaUuid": "a7181281-b2a9-31aa-80c4-8061c7c3abb5", "description": "PX4 Autopilot through 1.17.0 contains a stack buffer over-read vulnerability in the netman system command that fails to validate interface name length. Attackers can supply interface names of 74 bytes or more via the -i option to read beyond buffer boundaries, leaking stack memory to console output or writing it into persistent network configuration files.", "datePublished": "2026-09-08T11:23:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-14T19:33:06", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot/pull/28483", "https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot/commit/fec216e9d716d96d93b9d882b0c9cf00db3c6810", "https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot", "https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot/blob/v1.17.0/src/systemcmds/netman/netman.cpp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/px4-autopilot-through-1.17.0-stack-buffer-over-read-via-netman"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-86714", "GHSA-6x78-rh4h-q7jx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ac9ef648-62d6-3d31-889e-039f401a5103", "product": {"name": "PX4-Autopilot", "vendor": {"name": "PX4"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.17.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8d3ee7fc-dd22-3a3c-900e-b0967d4d074c", "vendor": {"name": "PX4"}}], "isExploited": false}